#: includes/views/getting-started/data-privacy.php:3
#: includes/views/getting-started/index.php:63
msgid "Data Privacy"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/getting-started/data-privacy.php:4
msgid "Information about the Data and Privacy"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/getting-started/data-privacy.php:10
msgid "Plugin authorization flow (OAuth)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/getting-started/data-privacy.php:12
msgid ""
"For technical reasons, the short-lived authorization code generated by the OAuth flow sent by your\n"
"                internet browser to our server as part of the authentication (OAuth) flow to provide the Application\n"
"                access to the Google Drive API."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/getting-started/data-privacy.php:18
msgid ""
"The Application obtains the following information when you use the built-in app for authentication and\n"
"                link the Application with your Google Drive Account:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/getting-started/data-privacy.php:23
msgid "Your WordPress website address."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/getting-started/data-privacy.php:24
msgid "A short-lived authorization code generated by the OAuth flow."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/getting-started/data-privacy.php:28
msgid ""
"This information is obtained and used after you decide to grand the Application the requested access via\n"
"                the Google OAuth consent screen. After giving the consent, you will be redirected to the server of\n"
"                softlabbd.com (https://softlabbd.com/integrate-google-drive-oauth.php) which will redirect you back to your\n"
"                own site where the authorization process is finalized. This redirect via the server of softlabbd.com is\n"
"                required for any easy plugin setup where you don’t need to create your own Google App which also allows\n"
"                you to set your own Authorized redirect URI. SoftLab Privacy Policy"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/getting-started/data-privacy.php:37
msgid ""
"On your own server, the short-lived authorization code will be exchanged for the actual access token and\n"
"                refresh token which are stored, encrypted, on your server. The authorization code can only be used once\n"
"                and will immediately become inactive after it has been exchanged for the access token or within minutes\n"
"                if it is not used."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/getting-started/data-privacy.php:44
msgid "IMPORTANT:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/getting-started/data-privacy.php:44
msgid ""
"When you use the Application, all other communications are strictly between\n"
"                your server and the cloud storage service servers. The communication is encrypted and the communication\n"
"                will not go through our servers. We do not collect and do not have access to your files."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/getting-started/data-privacy.php:53
msgid "Google Permissions for OAuth"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/getting-started/data-privacy.php:55
msgid ""
"In order for the Application to work seamlessly, Google Drive permission is granted by users during the\n"
"                standard oAuth authorization flow. Please see their privacy policies for further details"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/getting-started/data-privacy.php:60
msgid ""
"The Application uses the Google Drive permissions to allow it to see, edit, create, and delete all of\n"
"                your Google Drive files on your WordPress site. This is the core functionality of the plugin to make the\n"
"                integration between Google Drive and WordPress as seamless as possible. We ask for the ‘see’ permission\n"
"                to be able to list your files. The ‘create’ permission is used for uploading new content to your Google\n"
"                Drive. The other permissions are required to manage your files on Google Drive which includes, renaming,\n"
"                editing, deleting and sharing your files. Google Drive Privacy Policy and Terms of Use"
msgstr ""

